+prove canonical read-back, outer-whitespace invariance, omit-self identity
+order independence, and successful verification of every accepted generated
+identity. The checked-in cross-platform golden runs equivalent LF and CRLF
+representations with different property orders against one language-neutral
+SHA-256 identity. Validation uses fixed `100x` budgets and one worker per fuzz
+target so the gate is bounded by an input count rather than wall-clock timing.
+
